              <div class="tuf-authenticate">
                <h1 class="h__toc" id="/">City of Baltimore Law Library</h1>
                <section class="line-group annotations">
                  <h2>About This Website</h2>
                  <p><a href="/">codes.baltimorecity.gov</a> is the official home for the laws, regulations, and administrative policies of the <a href="https://www.baltimorecity.gov/">City of Baltimore</a>. It is edited and published by the <a href="https://www.baltimorecity.gov/legislative-reference">Department of Legislative Reference</a>.</p>
                  <p>This site makes City law easier to search, browse, and cite, allowing visitors to find what they need without knowing in advance where it lives.</p>
                  <p>For pending legislation and upcoming City Council meetings, the Council maintains its official legislative information system at <a href="https://baltimore.legistar.com/">baltimore.legistar.com</a>.</p>
                </section>
